    - target: {fileID: 7121630907809373752, guid: 4395306e5dcd4a749a31ec53a8235f05, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: The sampir or the upper part of the sheath most likely features Bhoma
        with his fierce face, bulging eyes, and gaping mouth. Similar to the Kirtimukha
        motif in South Indian temple architecture, Bhoma is traditionally depicted
        above Balinese Hindu temple entrances for protection and purification. The
        use of ivory for the sampir makes this elaborate scene showcasing multiple
        figures even more prominent.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7877242994502666739, guid: 4395306e5dcd4a749a31ec53a8235f05, type: 3}
